  "data_abstract": "Two-pion correlations in $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ =130 GeV Au+Au collisions at RHIC have been measured over a broad range of pair transverse momentum $k_T$ by the PHENIX experiment at RHIC. The $k_T$ dependent transverse radii are similar to results from heavy ion collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}}$ = 4.1, 4.9, and 17.3 GeV, whereas the longitudinal radius increases monotonically with beam energy. The ratio of the outwards to sidewards transverse radii ($R_{out}/R_{side}$) is consistent with unity and independent of $k_T$.\n",
